Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: SSH reverse tunnel client for NAT traversal
 NSSH is a lightweight SSH reverse tunnel client written in Go. It allows you
 to expose local services behind NAT or firewalls to the public internet
 through a standard OpenSSH server (sshd).
 .
 It speaks the SSH protocol natively, so no dedicated server component is
 required: connect straight to any OpenSSH host you already manage. Features
 include auto-reconnect with a configurable delay, heartbeat keep-alive,
 a background daemon that manages multiple tunnels, and password or SSH-key
 authentication.
